  },
  "proofCeiling": "This contribution proves pinned donor/source integrity including referenced companions, scoped harness infrastructure, deterministic interpreter continuity, ASB skill ownership/routing, schemas, ticket gates/frontier/spec-readiness logic, tracker command construction, public-plan boundaries and hosted/offline validators. It does not prove live GitHub permissions, actual human HITL answers/verdicts, research correctness beyond evidence, prototype usefulness, child-repository adoption, destination implementation or deployment.",
  "mustNotCopyOrReimplement": [
    "Do not treat public-plan tasks as a second copy of Wayfinder decision tickets.",
    "Do not put a full decision answer in both the map/public plan and its decision ticket; the ticket owns the detail.",
    "Do not allow an agent to satisfy prototype or grilling HITL gates with its own recommendation or inferred approval.",
    "Do not turn Wayfinder decision tickets into implementation tracer-bullet tickets; use to-tickets only after clarity.",
    "Do not make the temporary spec the durable source of decision rationale; retain ticket history.",
    "Do not install validation dependencies into a different Python interpreter than nested Wayfinder validators execute.",
    "Do not edit imported donor snapshots in place or auto-update the donor pin.",
    "Do not make child repositories depend directly on mattpocock/skills; adoption requires explicit review."
  ],
